  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Physical Description
    
    A perfect circle of aurora-glass, three hand-spans across, set in a frame of silver-ice that does not frost. The needle does not spin freely. It locks toward sources of captured fire with sufficient force to produce an audible hum — described consistently across accounts as resembling ice fracturing under pressure. One edge is pitted where aurora-light and forge-fire met during the Breach and scorched the glass. The needle was bent slightly during the Thaw and has never been straightened.
    
    ## Origin and Intended Purpose
    
    Forged during the Frozen Peace, Xueshei's Compass was conceived as an instrument of the Way∴ens ideology — the doctrine that fire-core knowledge should flow freely rather than remain under Fire Keeper monopoly. Its designed function was to guide miners to the Nightshelf's volcanic veins, facilitating cross-cultural trade. That it became something else is not the compass's failure.
    
    ## The Breach
    
    Plunge-Caller Oeichowei the Storm-Caller, then leader of the Pinnacle splinter faction, carried the compass into the Breach — the cascading conflict at Terrace Momiou triggered when the Qingqe'frostlings moved to claim the instrument by force against ☽'shadow Covens' Order. Oeichowei used its readings to locate the Order's fire-stores, burning three caverns and collapsing a tunnel system. The chronicles report forty-three dead, most of them miners working the deep shafts when the conflagration reached them. The figure is oddly specific for a tunnel collapse where recovery was incomplete, but I have no ice-memory counter-reading to offer.
    
    ## Current Status
    
    The compass is held by the Qingqe'frostlings, the governing council that consolidated control of Promenade Hei after the Orca Incursion. It sits in their war-hall wrapped in frost-cloth, unused. Those who have attempted to carry it report the needle pulling toward distant fires with enough force to cause pain, accompanied by dreams of drowning in heat. Oeichowei herself reportedly abandoned it at a memorial following the Shelf succession crisis and did not return.
    
    ## The Nyla Audit
    
    When unwrapped during an audit of the Midnight Claws' smuggling network — the investigation surrounding Shadow-Broker Nyla's confession — the needle locked toward the Nightshelf with force sufficient to drag its frame across stone. Its readings confirmed every fire-core cache and diversion route Nyla had already confessed to. At least one auditor noted the precision was troubling: the compass appeared to verify only what had been laid before it, as though it detected fire-memory held in living tissue rather than independently locating concealed stores. Whether this constitutes confirmation or theater depends on assumptions about the instrument's mechanism that no one has tested, because no one wishes to unwrap it again.
