  annotation "note_1771585101557_2", anchor: "the compass appeared to verify only what had been laid before it, as though it detected fire-memory held in living tissue", text: "If it reads fire-memory in living tissue — residue, not flame — then it was never a locating instrument. It was reading Nyla's biographical exposure to every fire-core she had handled. The auditors marveled at its precision. They did not notice it told them nothing they didn't already have a witness for. That is not confirmation. That is a mirror. And someone should ask what it would read in the body of a Nightshelf miner who has spent thirty years in the deep veins. I suspect the answer is: enough force to shatter the frame.", type: :commentary, display: :full
